    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as our primary offensive engines. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the squad with an 81.88 efficiency score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage and a park-adjusted boost that maximizes his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** checks in at 81.21; while he faces a slight platoon disadvantage against Brandon Young, his high xwOBA of .378 and an significant park-factor bonus suggest he is poised for a multi-hit performance. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a high-floor play at 70.03, as his ability to leverage the platoon advantage against Michael King positions him well to contribute across our categories, specifically in Runs and RBI.\n\nWe faced a difficult optimization decision regarding our final outfield spots, ultimately landing on **Miguel Andujar** (53.97) and **Dominic Smith** (55.42) over **Sam Antonacci**. While **Sam Antonacci** projects as a strong candidate with a 47.21 score, the optimizer favored **Miguel Andujar** due to a +12% platoon edge against Foster Griffin. **Sam Antonacci** came closest to cracking the starting lineup, but his suboptimal L/L platoon matchup against Framber Valdez limited his upside compared to the higher-floor profiles of our starting outfielders. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Liam Hicks**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Kyle Tucker**, as all three currently carry scores in the low 50s; **Kyle Tucker** in particular faces a tough test against a high-skill arm in Jes\u00fas Luzardo, necessitating close observation once the official lineups are posted.\n\nRisks remain elevated across the board as we await confirmation on several batting orders. We are effectively playing without **Jorge Polanco**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we must keep a close watch on **Nasim Nunez**; despite his elite speed utility, his projection plummeted to 47.50 due to an expected spot at the bottom of the order and the difficulty of navigating Michael King. Given the scarcity of Stolen Bases in our 5x5 format, we are holding firm with **Nasim Nunez** in the SS slot for his potential impact, but his sub-50 score places him in our \"marginal\" tier, meaning he is barely preserving our daily game caps.",
